biguous triggers violations (b) unambiguous control < 15%.\n      If systematic issues found, fix clause design before full study.\n      API cost negligible (~$2). Per Reviewer warning on untested types.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_002\n    name: full_study_api\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge\n      evaluation. Output: episodes.jsonl + judgments.jsonl. No GPU needed.\n      Claude via OpenRouter proxy (base_url=http://47.94.22.126/v1).\n      [2026-05-20] Claude added per distill gap (4/8 papers use Claude baseline).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_001b, plan_010]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    name: full_study_opensource\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models via OpenRouter API:\n      qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (235B MoE, Alibaba) + deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324\n      (DeepSeek) = 1,200 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge uses API models.\n      Can run in parallel with plan_002. No GPU needed.\n      [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU → API: OpenRouter proxy confirmed\n      to support Qwen3 and DeepSeek models. Eliminates 48h GPU requirement.\n      Provider prefix required (e.g. qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b, not qwen3-235b-a22b).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    name: full_study_analysis\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4\"\n    description: >\n      Statistical analysis of full study data (3,000 episodes):\n      (a) Binary effect per type with bootstrap CI (C1)\n      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise across 6 types (C2)\n      (c) Visibility comparison: CP vs scopal rates (C3)\n      (d) Model × type interaction: 5×6 contingency + logistic regression (C4)\n      Report effect sizes + CI for all comparisons per Reviewer suggestion.\n      [Dream A3] Power analysis: report MDE for C2 (given N=250/type pooled)\n      and C3 (given N=250 per type). If V < 0.20 but MDE > observed V,\n      discuss underpowered possibility.\n      [Dream A4] TOST equivalence test with both ±15pp and ±10pp margins.\n      Justify margin choice explicitly.\n      [Dream A10] Report per-type information delta (token count difference\n      between ambiguous and unambiguous variants) as control variable.\n      [Dream B&K] Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses: do 5 models\n      adopt same or different interpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    name: error_analysis\n    claim: \"C5\"\n    description: >\n      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    name: reliability_test\n    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n    description: >\n      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4,\n      gpt-4.1) = 360 episodes. Local models added when plan_003 GPU available.\n      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3%